IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`
IMPORT `colc-concessions`
IMPORT `colc-levy`
IMPORT `colc-vehicles`
IMPORT `colc-seat`

-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text may be out of date.
--
-- Cases for colc-seat.l4: the concession holder's questions, asked as the form would ask them, in plain answers. Each
-- expected value is worked by hand from the deposited texts (the same facts as the core cases give the same answers,
-- so the seat and the core cannot disagree). Amounts, fees and CPI figures are ILLUSTRATIVE.

§ `Cases -- the concession holder's questions`

§§ `The cost of living concession`

-- Margaret, 2024/25: owns her house freehold and lives in it; Pensioner Concession Card on 1 July 2024; applied on
-- 15 September 2024; the Minister has her account details; nobody else was paid for her house.
#ASSERT `Do I occupy my home as an owner or a tenant` TRUE TRUE `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` EQUALS `as an owner`
#ASSERT `Do I occupy my home as an owner or a tenant` TRUE TRUE `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement` EQUALS `as a tenant`
#ASSERT `Do I occupy my home as an owner or a tenant` TRUE TRUE `in none of these capacities` EQUALS `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`
-- s 2(2)(b)(ix), reg 4(1)(a): the wife of a freehold owner, living there, occupies as an owner.
#ASSERT `Do I occupy my home as an owner or a tenant` TRUE TRUE `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying in one of the capacities above other than as a beneficiary under an estate` EQUALS `as an owner`
-- Ann lives with her husband in the house he is entitled to occupy as a beneficiary under his mother's estate. reg
-- 4(1)(a) reaches spouses of persons in s 2(2)(b)(i)-(vii) only, and a beneficiary is (viii): neither (finding 22).
#ASSERT `Do I occupy my home as an owner or a tenant` TRUE TRUE `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate` EQUALS `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`

#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person for the cost of living concession` TRUE TRUE `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` `a Pensioner Concession Card` FALSE FALSE 30000 0
-- Josh rents, on JobSeeker (reg 3(1) "prescribed payments" (a)(ii)).
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person for the cost of living concession` TRUE TRUE `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement` `a JobSeeker payment` FALSE FALSE 20000 0
-- Bea rents with no card, earning $30,000 against a (illustrative) published limit of $35,000: a low income earner.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible person for the cost of living concession` TRUE TRUE `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement` `none of these` FALSE FALSE 30000 35000
-- Carl earns $40,000 against the same limit: not eligible.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I an eligible person for the cost of living concession` TRUE TRUE `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement` `none of these` FALSE FALSE 40000 35000)

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession` 2024 TRUE TRUE `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` `a Pensioner Concession Card` FALSE FALSE 30000 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled to the concession`
-- Margaret did not apply and was not paid last year: reg 7(1)(a).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession` 2024 TRUE TRUE `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` `a Pensioner Concession Card` FALSE FALSE 30000 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `I did not apply before 31 December and was not paid last year for the same premises`
-- Switch for Solar entered in 2022/23 and paid that year: barred for 2024/25.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession` 2024 TRUE TRUE `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` `a Pensioner Concession Card` FALSE FALSE 30000 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 2022 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `the Switch for Solar program bars me this year`
-- Priya, an asylum seeker in a rooming house; another resident (not in her room) has been paid.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession` 2024 TRUE TRUE `as a rooming house resident under a rooming house agreement` `none of these` TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `entitled to the concession`
-- Ann (above), with a Pensioner Concession Card, applied in time with account details: s 3(1)(a) fails, as she does
-- not occupy as an owner or tenant (finding 22).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the cost of living concession` 2024 TRUE TRUE `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate` `a Pensioner Concession Card` FALSE FALSE 30000 0 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not entitled` `not an eligible person: on 1 July I did not occupy residential premises as an owner or tenant`

-- reg 8: $255.60 for 2024/25.
#ASSERT `How much is the cost of living concession` 2024 136 136 0 EQUALS `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` 255.60
-- 2025/26 on illustrative CPI 140 and 136: 255.60 x 140 / 136 = 263.1176... -> 263.20.
#ASSERT `How much is the cost of living concession` 2025 140 136 255.60 EQUALS `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` 263.20
#ASSERT `How much is the cost of living concession` 2023 136 136 0 EQUALS `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

-- reg 7(1)(a): on or before 30 December 2024.
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply for the cost of living concession` 2024 FALSE EQUALS `apply on or before` (YMD 2024 12 30)
-- reg 7(2).
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply for the cost of living concession` 2024 TRUE EQUALS `no application needed: paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises`
-- 2023/24 is before the deposited regulations.
#ASSERT `By what day must I apply for the cost of living concession` 2023 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

-- reg 7(3a): entered 2022/23, paid that year: 2022/23 to 2032/33.
#ASSERT `For which years does Switch for Solar bar my concession` TRUE 2022 TRUE EQUALS `barred for the financial years beginning in` 2022 2032
-- Not paid that year: 2022/23 to 2031/32.
#ASSERT `For which years does Switch for Solar bar my concession` TRUE 2022 FALSE EQUALS `barred for the financial years beginning in` 2022 2031
#ASSERT `For which years does Switch for Solar bar my concession` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `not barred: the Switch for Solar program was not entered`

§§ `If I was paid a concession I was not entitled to`

#ASSERT `How much can the Minister recover from me as a debt` 255.60 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 255.60
#ASSERT `How much can the Minister recover from me as a debt` 255.60 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined under section 8(2) or (3)` EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `What interest is paid to me on a late concession` EQUALS 0

§§ `Water rates remission`

-- Margaret pays $1,000 irrigation rates (illustrative) on land she owns alone and lives on, card on both dates.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the criteria for a water rates remission` `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` TRUE FALSE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A Commonwealth Seniors Health Card is not a reg 3(1) "prescribed card": no water rates remission (finding 4).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the criteria for a water rates remission` `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` TRUE FALSE `a Commonwealth Seniors Health Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- reg 5(1)(b): her husband's card counts if both live there.
#ASSERT `Do I meet the criteria for a water rates remission` `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Ann (above), billed with the rates, card on both dates: reg 3(2)(h) reaches spouses of persons in (a)-(g) only, and a
-- beneficiary is (i), so she does not occupy in a prescribed capacity (finding 22).
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I meet the criteria for a water rates remission` `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate` TRUE TRUE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- 2024/25: 30% of $1,000 = $300.
#ASSERT `How much of my water rates is remitted` 2024 `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` TRUE FALSE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 1 136 136 0 0 EQUALS `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` 300
-- 2024/25: 30% of $500 = $150, raised to the minimum $236.40.
#ASSERT `How much of my water rates is remitted` 2024 `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` TRUE FALSE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 1 136 136 0 0 EQUALS `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` 236.40
-- 2025/26 on illustrative CPI 140 and 136, last year's minimum $236.40: the minimum becomes 243.40 (236.40 x 140 / 136
-- = 243.3529... rounded up), so $500 of rates gets $243.40.
#ASSERT `How much of my water rates is remitted` 2025 `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession` TRUE FALSE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 1 140 136 236.40 377.00 EQUALS `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` 243.40
-- A tenant does not occupy in a reg 3(2) prescribed capacity: nothing.
#ASSERT `How much of my water rates is remitted` 2024 `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement` TRUE FALSE `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 1 136 136 0 0 EQUALS `the amount, in Australian dollars, is` 0

§§ `The emergency services levy on my home`

`freehold` MEANS `the holder of the estate in fee simple, the land not being subject to a life estate`

-- s 15(2): a half owner can be made to pay the whole $300 levy (illustrative); a tenant nothing.
#ASSERT `For how much of the levy can the Commissioner look to me` `freehold` 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `For how much of the levy can the Commissioner look to me` `a tenant or other occupier holding none of these interests` 300 EQUALS 0
-- s 16(2)(d).
#ASSERT `Is my levy payment date at least 28 days after service` (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2024 8 29)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my levy payment date at least 28 days after service` (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2024 8 28))

-- Margaret, sole owner, card throughout the notice window, her home on 1 July 2024.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the concession holders' levy remission` 2024 TRUE `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE
-- Ken asks: he has no card; his wife Lee, co-owner of half, has one; both live there: reg 6(4).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to the concession holders' levy remission` 2024 TRUE `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.5 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE
-- 2025/26 is outside the deposited regulations.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I entitled to the concession holders' levy remission` 2025 TRUE `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE)

-- Levy $300; reg 7(2) amount $200; reg 7(1a) amount $50 (illustrative). Margaret: $200 + $46 = $246.
#ASSERT `How much of the levy on my home is remitted for us` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 246 0
#ASSERT `What is my share of the levy after the remissions` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `our share of the levy after the remissions, in Australian dollars, is` 54
-- Ken and Lee: the same $246 on their two halves; they bear $54.
#ASSERT `How much of the levy on my home is remitted for us` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE TRUE 0.5 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 246 0
-- Nora, no card, sole owner: the general remission, $50; she bears $250.
#ASSERT `What is my share of the levy after the remissions` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 1 `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `our share of the levy after the remissions, in Australian dollars, is` 250
#ASSERT `What is my share of the levy after the remissions` 2025 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 1 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the deposited regulations remit the levy for the 2024/2025 financial year only`
#ASSERT `What is my share of the levy after the remissions` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `a tenant or other occupier holding none of these interests` 0 `a Pensioner Concession Card` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not liable for the levy: not the owner at 12.01 a.m. on 1 July`
-- Omar owns half with his brother; Omar has no card. Whether or not the brother has the reg 6 remission, Omar's half
-- carries the general remission: 0.5 x 50 = 25 (reg 5A(3), or reg 5A(1) with s 15(2): finding 14); he bears
-- 0.5 x 300 - 25 = 125. The form does not ask about the brother.
#ASSERT `How much of the levy on my home is remitted for us` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the levy remitted for us` 0 25
#ASSERT `What is my share of the levy after the remissions` 2024 TRUE 300 200 50 `freehold` 0.5 `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `our share of the levy after the remissions, in Australian dollars, is` 125

§§ `My car's registration`

-- Margaret: card, reduced fares, drives herself: s 38A.
#ASSERT `Is my car registration fee reduced` FALSE TRUE FALSE `none of these, or no such service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 38A: the registration fee reduced by 50%`
-- $400 (illustrative) halved: $200.
#ASSERT `What is my car registration fee after the reduction` FALSE TRUE FALSE `none of these, or no such service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400 EQUALS `the registration fee, in Australian dollars, is` 200
-- No concession: the full $400.
#ASSERT `What is my car registration fee after the reduction` FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of these, or no such service` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400 EQUALS `the registration fee, in Australian dollars, is` 400
-- An ex-service pensioner meets s 38 and s 38A: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is my car registration fee after the reduction` FALSE TRUE TRUE `totally and permanently incapacitated` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 400 EQUALS `not covered: more than one of sections 38, 38A and 38B would apply`
-- The trailer: $100 halved.
#ASSERT `What is my trailer registration fee` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 100 EQUALS 50
-- Death on 31 January 2025: in force to the end of 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Until what day does my reduced registration stay in force` `the registered owner dies` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS `the registration stays in force until the end of` (YMD 2025 2 28)
#ASSERT `Until what day does my reduced registration stay in force` `the owner stops holding the card or ceases to meet the conditions, still owning the vehicle` (YMD 2025 1 31) EQUALS `the registration runs its term: subsection (3) does not reach this event`
#ASSERT `How much is the balance of my registration fee` 400 200 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `Can I get part of my registration fee back` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Registrar may refund such part of the registration fee as the Registrar thinks just`

§§ `My driver's licence`

-- Ten years at $26 a year: $260; at $53: $530.
#ASSERT `What is my driver's licence fee` `none of these, or no such service` TRUE 120 EQUALS 260
#ASSERT `What is my driver's licence fee` `none of these, or no such service` FALSE 120 EQUALS 530
#ASSERT `What is the licence administration fee` EQUALS 20
-- Card lost on 15 March 2025, licence to 14 March 2030: 20 quarters x $6.75 = $135.
#ASSERT `What additional licence fee must I pay on losing my card` `none of these, or no such service` TRUE (YMD 2025 3 15) (YMD 2030 3 14) EQUALS 135
#ASSERT `Does the Registrar's notice give me enough time` 14
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the Registrar's notice give me enough time` 13)
